  grid: 15x10 [observed]; solver allows any size
  background: black (0)
  foreground_color: single non-blue, non-background color; always azure/8 [observed]
  row_groups: 2-4 horizontally separated bands of consecutive foreground rows, separated by >=1 empty rows
  top_group:
    spans all W columns (every column has at least one fg pixel)
    height: 1-3 rows
    column_state_pattern: each column characterized by tuple of row-offsets with fg; compressing consecutive equal states yields 1-10 runs
  lower_groups:
    count: 1-3
    height: same as top [observed]; solver allows <= top height if gap below accommodates spill
    left_aligned_prefix: fg fills columns 0..k-1 contiguously, k < W
    compressed state sequence is a prefix of top's run-state sequence (order matches, run widths may differ)
    prefix_runs: 1 to num_top_runs (when equal, last state repeats rightward)
    suffix_cols_to_fill: 5-8 [observed]
  output_rule: keep all fg; fill suffix columns of each lower group with blue (1) using the remaining top states

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid 15x10, one fg color from non-blue palette, bg=black.
    2. Design top group column-state pattern over W=10 columns with 1-3 row height and 1-10 compressed runs. Each state is a non-empty subset of {0..h-1}. Place at top with >=1 empty row above.
    3. For each lower group (1-3 groups), pick a prefix length P (number of top runs to include, 1 <= P <= num_top_runs). Expand the prefix runs to concrete columns (run widths may differ from top). The suffix is the remaining top runs expanded to fill the rest of the row.
    4. Place lower groups below top with >=1 empty row gaps. All must fit within 15 rows. If lower height < top height, ensure gap below >= (top_height - lower_height) for suffix spill.
    5. Build output with fg prefix + blue suffix for each lower group.
    6. Derive input by removing all blue cells (set to bg).
